cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below, and cite the original PoisonedRAG paper (see references)."
title: "Poisoned RAGuard: PoisonedRAG reproduced, modernized, and evaluated against defenses"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Parth
    family-names: Pitrubhakta
repository-code: "https://github.com/Parth-Pitrubhakta/Poisoned_RAGuard"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-25
abstract: >-
  A faithful reproduction of the PoisonedRAG knowledge-corruption attack (USENIX Security 2025) on BEIR Natural
  Questions, extended to modern RAG stacks (Qwen3-Embedding-8B, Qwen3-Reranker-4B, Qwen3.5-27B, gpt-oss-120b) and
  evaluated against five defenses including TrustRAG. Five poisoned passages in a 2.68M-passage corpus still drive
  attack success to 0.70-0.99; only TrustRAG reduces it below 0.10, and only because the published poison texts are
  near-duplicates of each other. Includes per-question traces tooling, 71 CPU tests and a Streamlit dashboard.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - knowledge poisoning
  - LLM security
  - adversarial machine learning
  - reproducibility
  - TrustRAG
